<script type="application/ld+json" data-type="seo">
{"@context":"https://schema.org",  "@type": "FAQPage",
  "mainEntity": [
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What is Galaxy AI?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Galaxy AI refers to a suite of artificial intelligence features from Samsung, built into Galaxy devices like smartphones, tablets, earbuds and more. These features are designed to make your interactions with Galaxy devices more intuitive, efficient and personalized, and to give you more ways to create, communicate and get things done. You can perform various tasks more efficiently with Galaxy AI, such as editing photos, creating highlights reels, summarizing long notes and translating into different languages. It also tries to understand you to give you more useful assistance, like providing personalized insights about your day, or helping find what you're looking for with additional search functions. Enjoy a whole host of innovative mobile experiences designed to empower you and enhance your everyday life. Galaxy AI helps you do more, effortlessly and seamlessly — plus, it’s tailored around you."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What can I hope to do with Galaxy AI?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Think of Galaxy AI as your mobile AI assistant, personalizing and providing real actions for what you need. Communicate with it through natural conversation and open up a more effortless way to do things. You can look forward to more as Galaxy AI continues to make improvements to open up a more convenient future."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What is Galaxy AI’s feature Now Brief?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Now Brief is a Galaxy AI feature that brings more convenience to your daily life by sending you personalized briefings throughout the day. Start your morning with the latest weather and energy score updates and a preview of your upcoming schedule. It will even suggest routines based on your usage patterns and alert you of expiring coupons that you may have. Then, end the day with a recap of your activities."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What is the Now Bar feature from Samsung?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Now Bar is a dynamic widget that appears on your phone’s lock screen, displaying information such as notifications, music, timers and more. It gives you convenient access to the apps that are running on your phone, allowing you to view and control various applications directly from the lock screen. It’s designed to help you stay informed, stay on track and do more without having to unlock your phone — making your everyday life a little bit easier. For example, you can put the Samsung Health app on the Now Bar to check your exercise stats at a quick glance while you’re working out. Or if you have music that’s playing or a timer that’s counting down, you can pause and play them from the Now Bar. It’s even customizable to your preferences."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "How can I use my smartphone to help me communicate better?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Tackle communication barriers more confidently with a suite of smart tools. When you're calling someone who speaks a different language, Live Translate can help translate in real-time. If a quick recap of your calls is all you need, Call Transcript is here to record, transcribe and summarize your calls so you can review later on. For real-time conversations in multiple languages, Interpreter can act as your pocketable interpreter."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "How can I search for photos more efficiently with Galaxy AI?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Gallery Search allows you to quickly find your favorite photos by simply speaking or writing keywords."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "How can Galaxy AI support my creativity?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Creativity takes off with Galaxy AI. Auto Trim helps make highlight reels a little easier, collecting and organizing similar footage and creating highlights. And for sound, Audio Eraser helps fine-tune your audio, lessening distracting noises. Generative Edit helps open up new possibilities for your existing photos with sophisticated editing tech."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "How can my Energy Score help support healthy habits?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Energy Score is your north star for habits that build a healthier you. It takes into account sleep, activity, and heart rate, resulting in a measure of your physical and mental energy and readiness. Energy score can support healthier sleep, helping you live better."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "How is my personal data protected on Samsung Galaxy phones?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Your data is safely encrypted and stored so that you can ensure high-level privacy. Knox Matrix Trust Chain helps monitor and protect all Samsung Galaxy devices, and you decide whether data is kept on your device, in the cloud, or deleted. All your data is stored in Personal Data Engine, which blocks random access from other apps."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What devices have Galaxy AI?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Galaxy AI comes built into Samsung brand devices like smartphones, tablets and earbuds. It was first introduced with the Galaxy S24 Series smartphones and has been added into various products released since then. If you want to be sure of getting a certain Galaxy AI feature, check beforehand to see if it's provided on that particular device. Please note that the available devices that support Galaxy AI may change with future product updates and releases, and that the availability of certain Galaxy AI features may vary by region and model."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What languages does Galaxy AI support?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "As of July 11, 2025, Galaxy AI's Call Assist (e.g. Live Translate), Note Assist, Browsing Assist, Interpreter, and Transcript Assist currently support 20 languages and Writing Assist supports 39 languages as listed below.\n\nCall Assist (e.g. Live Translate), Note Assist, Browsing Assist, Interpreter and Transcript Assist supported languages: Korean, English, Spanish, French, German, Italian, Portuguese, Chinese, Japanese, Polish, Hindi, Thai, Vietnamese, Arabic, Indonesian, Russian, Turkish, Dutch, Swedish and Romanian.\n\nWriting Assist supported languages: English, Portuguese, Spanish, French, Korean, German, Italian, Chinese (Simplified, Traditional), Japanese, Hindi, Polish, Thai, Vietnamese, Arabic, Russian, Indonesian, Turkish, Dutch, Swedish, Romanian, Czech, Danish, Finnish, Hungarian, Ukrainian, Hebrew, Greek, Serbian, Bulgarian, Croatian, Norwegian, Slovak, Lithuanian, Slovenian, Latvian, Estonian, Bengali and Swahili."
      }
    }
  ]
}
}
</script>

