	<ul class="su12-accordion-faqs  " role="list">
		
			
			
			<li class="su12-accordion-faqs__item on" an-tr="su12_accordion faqs-im marketing page-cta-content_click" an-ca="content click" an-ac="feature" an-la="faq:accordion:what devices have galaxy ai" role="listitem">
				<h3>
					<a href="javascript:void(0)" class="su12-accordion-faqs__title" aria-expanded="true" role="button">
						
						<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__title-text">What devices have Galaxy AI?</div>
						<span class="icon-wrap">
							<svg class="icon plus" focusable="false"><use xlink:href="#plus-bold" href="#plus-bold"></use></svg>
							<svg class="icon minus" focusable="false"><use xlink:href="#minus-bold" href="#minus-bold"></use></svg>
						</span>
					</a>
				</h3>
				<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents" id="anchor-id05">
					<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents-description">Galaxy AI comes built into Samsung devices like smartphones, smartwatches, earbuds and tablets, although the available features vary by device.
<br />
<br />⦁ Galaxy AI is supported on smartphones starting from the S24 Series phones onward.
<br />⦁ Galaxy AI is supported on tablets and wearable products (such as Galaxy Watch and Galaxy Buds), but the level of support depends on the model and OS version.
<br />⦁ The availability of certain Galaxy AI features may vary by region as well as model. If you want to be sure of getting a certain Galaxy AI feature, check beforehand that it's provided on that particular model in your region.
<br />⦁ Please note that the supported features and models may change with future product releases and updates.</div>
					
					
						
					<!--
						<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents-disclaimer-wrap">
							<p class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents-disclaimer">...omitted...</p>
						</div>-->
						
					

					
				</div>
			</li>
		
			
			
			<li class="su12-accordion-faqs__item " an-tr="su12_accordion faqs-im marketing page-cta-content_click" an-ca="content click" an-ac="feature" an-la="faq:accordion:how do i use galaxy ai on my samsung phone" role="listitem">
				<h3>
					<a href="javascript:void(0)" class="su12-accordion-faqs__title" aria-expanded="false" role="button">
						
						<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__title-text">How do I use Galaxy AI on my Samsung phone?</div>
						<span class="icon-wrap">
							<svg class="icon plus" focusable="false"><use xlink:href="#plus-bold" href="#plus-bold"></use></svg>
							<svg class="icon minus" focusable="false"><use xlink:href="#minus-bold" href="#minus-bold"></use></svg>
						</span>
					</a>
				</h3>
				<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents" id="anchor-id190">
					<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents-description">Galaxy AI comes built into various Samsung devices, though available features may vary by model. Some Galaxy AI features run automatically in the background, while others can be activated by tapping on the four-star Galaxy AI icon that appears in certain apps and screens.
<br />⦁ Some Galaxy AI features run automatically by default, making them effortless to enjoy.
<br />⦁ Some Galaxy AI features require user action. Tap the Galaxy AI icon that appears in certain apps and screens to bring up a list of relevant actions. Then tap the action you want, and it will be done for you instantly.
<br />⦁ Certain Galaxy AI features can be customized to your preferences, so you can adjust to the experience you want. In addition to enabling and disabling features, you can choose how they function in certain situations and more.</div>
					
					
						
					<!--
						<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents-disclaimer-wrap">
							<p class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents-disclaimer">...omitted...</p>
						</div>-->
						
					

					
				</div>
			</li>
		
			
			
			<li class="su12-accordion-faqs__item " an-tr="su12_accordion faqs-im marketing page-cta-content_click" an-ca="content click" an-ac="feature" an-la="faq:accordion:what are the main features of samsung is galaxy ai" role="listitem">
				<h3>
					<a href="javascript:void(0)" class="su12-accordion-faqs__title" aria-expanded="false" role="button">
						
						<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__title-text">What are the main features of Samsung’s Galaxy AI?</div>
						<span class="icon-wrap">
							<svg class="icon plus" focusable="false"><use xlink:href="#plus-bold" href="#plus-bold"></use></svg>
							<svg class="icon minus" focusable="false"><use xlink:href="#minus-bold" href="#minus-bold"></use></svg>
						</span>
					</a>
				</h3>
				<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents" id="anchor-id272">
					<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents-description">Galaxy AI provides a wide variety of features for personalization, productivity, creativity and communication, with some of the more prominent features being:
<br />⦁ Photo Assist: Powerful editing tools in your Gallery that let you effortlessly get your photos looking the way you want.
<br />⦁ Creative Studio: Creation tools that let you easily make custom content like personalized stickers.
<br />⦁ Now Nudge: Recognizes what's happening on your screen to provide context-aware suggestions for your convenience, like shortcuts to your Calendar and Gallery apps.
<br />⦁ Now Brief: Quick snapshots of useful info and insights delivered throughout the day to help keep you on track, including news, calendar events and personal recaps, along with personalized reminders and recommendations.
<br />⦁ Interpreter: Real-time translations are delivered as audio to your Galaxy Buds and as text on your Galaxy phone.
<br />⦁ Writing Assist: A writing and editing tool that lets you proofread, reformat, reword and summarize any text you’ve written or selected.
<br />⦁ Bixby: A personal device assistant capable of natural, free-flowing conversation.<sup>1,2,5,6,10,12,15</sup></div>
					
					
						
					<!--
						<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents-disclaimer-wrap">
							<p class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents-disclaimer">...omitted...</p>
						</div>-->
						
					

					
				</div>
			</li>
		
			
			
			<li class="su12-accordion-faqs__item " an-tr="su12_accordion faqs-im marketing page-cta-content_click" an-ca="content click" an-ac="feature" an-la="faq:accordion:what are the key galaxy ai features of samsung galaxy s26 ultra" role="listitem">
				<h3>
					<a href="javascript:void(0)" class="su12-accordion-faqs__title" aria-expanded="false" role="button">
						
						<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__title-text">What are the key Galaxy AI features of Samsung Galaxy S26 Ultra?</div>
						<span class="icon-wrap">
							<svg class="icon plus" focusable="false"><use xlink:href="#plus-bold" href="#plus-bold"></use></svg>
							<svg class="icon minus" focusable="false"><use xlink:href="#minus-bold" href="#minus-bold"></use></svg>
						</span>
					</a>
				</h3>
				<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents" id="anchor-id319">
					<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents-description">Samsung Galaxy S26 Ultra is powered by Galaxy AI to provide a smoother, more intelligent mobile experience and various tools for creation, communication, productivity and more, with some of the key features including:
<br />
<br />⦁ Photo Assist, which provides powerful image editing and creation tools for your photos.
<br />⦁ Creative Studio, which lets you easily create custom content like personalized sticker sets.
<br />⦁ Now Nudge, which recognizes what's happening on your screen to provide context-aware suggestions for your convenience, like shortcuts to your Calendar and Gallery apps.
<br />⦁ Now Brief, which organizes insights and updates about your day in short, efficient briefs, allowing you to easily catch up on calendar events, news items, your daily activity and more, along with personalized reminders and recommendations.
<br />⦁ Document Scan, which automatically detects and cleans up pictures of documents taken from your phone.
<br />⦁ Bixby, Samsung’s personal device assistant that lets you give commands and ask for advice using natural language.<sup>1,2,5,6,11,15,18</sup></div>
					
					
						
					<!--
						<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents-disclaimer-wrap">
							<p class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents-disclaimer">...omitted...</p>
						</div>-->
						
					

					
				</div>
			</li>
		
			
			
			<li class="su12-accordion-faqs__item " an-tr="su12_accordion faqs-im marketing page-cta-content_click" an-ca="content click" an-ac="feature" an-la="faq:accordion:what are the benefits of samsung galaxy ai for everyday users like me" role="listitem">
				<h3>
					<a href="javascript:void(0)" class="su12-accordion-faqs__title" aria-expanded="false" role="button">
						
						<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__title-text">What are the benefits of Samsung Galaxy AI for everyday users like me?</div>
						<span class="icon-wrap">
							<svg class="icon plus" focusable="false"><use xlink:href="#plus-bold" href="#plus-bold"></use></svg>
							<svg class="icon minus" focusable="false"><use xlink:href="#minus-bold" href="#minus-bold"></use></svg>
						</span>
					</a>
				</h3>
				<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents" id="anchor-id484">
					<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents-description">Galaxy AI makes your devices more intelligent, intuitive and context-aware, so they’re able to support you more naturally in everyday tasks and provide real actions for what you need. Not only that, Galaxy AI powers a wide range of useful tools and features that let you accomplish more tasks and work more efficiently on your device.
<br />⦁ Context-aware assistance: Galaxy AI helps your device understand what’s going on, resulting in smarter assistance that helps streamline tasks and save time. For example, Now Nudge provides quick action prompts based on what it recognizes is happening on your screen.
<br />⦁ Additional tools and features: Galaxy AI powers a whole host of additional features within your device, including creative tools like Photo Assist and Creative Studio, productivity tools like Transcript Assist and Writing Assist and communication tools like Interpreter.
<br />⦁ More personalized insights: Galaxy AI also powers your device to provide more intelligent insights about yourself. You can get useful reminders and recaps about your day with Now Brief and deeper insights about your health in Energy Score.<sup>1,2,5,6,9,12,14</sup></div>
					
					
						
					<!--
						<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents-disclaimer-wrap">
							<p class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents-disclaimer">...omitted...</p>
						</div>-->
						
					

					
				</div>
			</li>
		
			
			
			<li class="su12-accordion-faqs__item " an-tr="su12_accordion faqs-im marketing page-cta-content_click" an-ca="content click" an-ac="feature" an-la="faq:accordion:what languages does galaxy ai support" role="listitem">
				<h3>
					<a href="javascript:void(0)" class="su12-accordion-faqs__title" aria-expanded="false" role="button">
						
						<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__title-text">What languages does Galaxy AI support?</div>
						<span class="icon-wrap">
							<svg class="icon plus" focusable="false"><use xlink:href="#plus-bold" href="#plus-bold"></use></svg>
							<svg class="icon minus" focusable="false"><use xlink:href="#minus-bold" href="#minus-bold"></use></svg>
						</span>
					</a>
				</h3>
				<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents" id="anchor-id590">
					<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents-description">As of March 2026, Galaxy AI's Photo Assist, Creative Studio and Writing Assist support 41 languages. Now Nudge and Recalled data for Now Brief support 13 languages. Call Assist (e.g. Live Translate), Note Assist, Interpreter, and Transcript Assist support 22 languages. Call Screening feature for Call Assist supports 13 languages.
<br />
<br />Full list of languages is below.
<br />
<br />⦁ Photo Assist supported languages: English, Spanish, Portuguese, German, French, Italian, Polish, Korean, Chinese (Simplified, Traditional), Japanese, Thai, Vietnamese, Arabic, Indonesian, Hindi, Russian, Turkish, Romanian, Swedish, Dutch, Czech, Danish, Finnish, Hungarian, Ukrainian, Hebrew, Greek, Serbian, Bulgarian, Croatian, Norwegian, Slovak, Lithuanian, Slovenian, Latvian, Estonian, Bengali, Swahili, Filipino and Gujarati.
<br />⦁ Creative Studio supported languages: English, Spanish, Portuguese, German, French, Italian, Polish, Korean, Chinese (Simplified, Traditional), Japanese, Thai, Vietnamese, Arabic, Indonesian, Hindi, Russian, Turkish, Romanian, Swedish, Dutch, Czech, Danish, Finnish, Hungarian, Ukrainian, Hebrew, Greek, Serbian, Bulgarian, Croatian, Norwegian, Slovak, Lithuanian, Slovenian, Latvian, Estonian, Bengali, Swahili, Filipino and Gujarati.
<br />⦁ Now Nudge supported languages: Korean, English, Spanish, Italian, German, French, Portuguese, Polish, Chinese (Simplified), Japanese, Thai, Hindi and Vietnamese.
<br />⦁ Recalled data for Now Brief supported languages: Korean, English, Spanish, Italian, German, French, Portuguese, Polish, Chinese (Simplified), Japanese, Thai, Hindi and Vietnamese.
<br />⦁ Call Assist (e.g. Live Translate), Note Assist, Interpreter, and Transcript Assist supported languages: Korean, English, Spanish, French, German, Italian, Portuguese, Chinese, Japanese, Polish, Hindi, Thai, Vietnamese, Arabic, Indonesian, Russian, Turkish, Dutch, Swedish, Romanian, Filipino and Gujarati.
<br />⦁ Call Screening feature for Call Assist supported languages: English, Portuguese, Spanish, French, German, Italian, Chinese (Simplified), Japanese, Korean, Thai, Polish, Vietnamese and Hindi.
<br />⦁ Writing Assist supported languages: English, Portuguese, Spanish, French, Korean, German, Italian, Chinese (Simplified, Traditional), Japanese, Hindi, Polish, Thai, Vietnamese, Arabic, Russian, Indonesian, Turkish, Dutch, Swedish, Romanian, Czech, Danish, Finnish, Hungarian, Ukrainian, Hebrew, Greek, Serbian, Bulgarian, Croatian, Norwegian, Slovak, Lithuanian, Slovenian, Latvian, Estonian, Bengali, Swahili, Filipino and Gujarati.</div>
					
					
						
					<!--
						<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents-disclaimer-wrap">
							<p class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents-disclaimer">...omitted...</p>
						</div>-->
						
					

					
				</div>
			</li>
		
			
			
			<li class="su12-accordion-faqs__item " an-tr="su12_accordion faqs-im marketing page-cta-content_click" an-ca="content click" an-ac="feature" an-la="faq:accordion:how does having a good ai phone improve my everyday mobile experiences" role="listitem">
				<h3>
					<a href="javascript:void(0)" class="su12-accordion-faqs__title" aria-expanded="false" role="button">
						
						<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__title-text">How does having a good AI phone improve my everyday mobile experiences?</div>
						<span class="icon-wrap">
							<svg class="icon plus" focusable="false"><use xlink:href="#plus-bold" href="#plus-bold"></use></svg>
							<svg class="icon minus" focusable="false"><use xlink:href="#minus-bold" href="#minus-bold"></use></svg>
						</span>
					</a>
				</h3>
				<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents" id="anchor-id629">
					<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents-description">A good AI phone helps everyday mobile experiences flow more smoothly by understanding your personal context to provide more intuitive interactions and personalized assistance. In addition, AI can unlock various features that let you do more on your phone, whether it’s for work tasks or personal creative pursuits. Here are a few ways Galaxy AI enhances the mobile experience on Samsung smartphones:
<br />⦁ Intuitive interactions: Galaxy AI helps your phone better understand what’s happening, so you can find or achieve what you need faster with features like Now Nudge. 
<br />⦁ Personalized assistance: Galaxy AI grasps your patterns and preferences to deliver information that’s more useful and relevant to you, like tailored insights with Now Brief and a more detailed Energy Score.
<br />⦁ Creative tools: Galaxy AI powers various creative tools like Photo Assist and Creative Studio, allowing you to edit, design and create like a professional on your phone.
<br />⦁ Productivity tools: Galaxy AI also powers various useful tools for work and study, like Transcript Assist and Writing Assist, which can help summarize and organize large amounts of information in no time.<sup>1,2,5,6,7,9,12,14</sup></div>
					
					
						
					<!--
						<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents-disclaimer-wrap">
							<p class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents-disclaimer">...omitted...</p>
						</div>-->
						
					

					
				</div>
			</li>
		
			
			
			<li class="su12-accordion-faqs__item " an-tr="su12_accordion faqs-im marketing page-cta-content_click" an-ca="content click" an-ac="feature" an-la="faq:accordion:how do samsung galaxy phones improve photo quality with ai" role="listitem">
				<h3>
					<a href="javascript:void(0)" class="su12-accordion-faqs__title" aria-expanded="false" role="button">
						
						<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__title-text">How do Samsung Galaxy phones improve photo quality with AI?</div>
						<span class="icon-wrap">
							<svg class="icon plus" focusable="false"><use xlink:href="#plus-bold" href="#plus-bold"></use></svg>
							<svg class="icon minus" focusable="false"><use xlink:href="#minus-bold" href="#minus-bold"></use></svg>
						</span>
					</a>
				</h3>
				<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents" id="anchor-id759">
					<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents-description">Samsung Galaxy phones improve photo quality with AI through the following methods:
<br />⦁ AI ProVisual Engine: Samsung’s advanced image processor is powered by AI to enhance photo quality. AI ProVisual Engine intelligently analyzes and refines every frame for clarity, color and detail. The result is stunningly accurate, true-to-life photos and videos, even when taken at night or from a distance.
<br />⦁ AI ISP: Samsung combines its Image Signal Processor (ISP) with AI to automatically optimize each shot in real time for clearer, more detailed images. AI ISP has now been applied to the front camera as well in Samsung Galaxy S26 Ultra to produce more natural, realistic selfies when pictures are snapped from the front.<sup>19</sup></div>
					
					
						
					<!--
						<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents-disclaimer-wrap">
							<p class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents-disclaimer">...omitted...</p>
						</div>-->
						
					

					
				</div>
			</li>
		
			
			
			<li class="su12-accordion-faqs__item " an-tr="su12_accordion faqs-im marketing page-cta-content_click" an-ca="content click" an-ac="feature" an-la="faq:accordion:how do i use the translation feature on samsung galaxy buds" role="listitem">
				<h3>
					<a href="javascript:void(0)" class="su12-accordion-faqs__title" aria-expanded="false" role="button">
						
						<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__title-text">How do I use the translation feature on Samsung Galaxy Buds?</div>
						<span class="icon-wrap">
							<svg class="icon plus" focusable="false"><use xlink:href="#plus-bold" href="#plus-bold"></use></svg>
							<svg class="icon minus" focusable="false"><use xlink:href="#minus-bold" href="#minus-bold"></use></svg>
						</span>
					</a>
				</h3>
				<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents" id="anchor-id863">
					<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents-description">To hear translations spoken directly into your Samsung Galaxy Buds, you can use the Interpreter feature through the following steps:
<br />⦁ Open the Interpreter app on your phone. You may have to download the appropriate language pack for the language of the person you’re speaking with.
<br />⦁ Place your Galaxy Buds in your ears.
<br />⦁ Tap the microphone icon that appears on your phone’s screen. In Listening Mode, the microphone icon appears at the bottom of the screen. In Conversation Mode, there are two microphone icons that appear on screen, one for each of the languages being translated.
<br />⦁ Allow the Interpreter app to listen to your conversation partner as they speak in a different language. You may have to select for your desired languages.
<br />⦁ The spoken translation will be delivered to your Galaxy Buds. In addition, the transcribed text will also be displayed on the screen of your phone, so you can read along as you listen.
<br />⦁ You can also pause, resume and play back the recording using the touch controls of your Galaxy Buds.<sup>10</sup></div>
					
					
						
					<!--
						<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents-disclaimer-wrap">
							<p class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents-disclaimer">...omitted...</p>
						</div>-->
						
					

					
				</div>
			</li>
		
			
			
			<li class="su12-accordion-faqs__item " an-tr="su12_accordion faqs-im marketing page-cta-content_click" an-ca="content click" an-ac="feature" an-la="faq:accordion:what are the latest ai upgrades for bixby on samsung galaxy phones" role="listitem">
				<h3>
					<a href="javascript:void(0)" class="su12-accordion-faqs__title" aria-expanded="false" role="button">
						
						<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__title-text">What are the latest AI upgrades for Bixby on Samsung Galaxy phones?</div>
						<span class="icon-wrap">
							<svg class="icon plus" focusable="false"><use xlink:href="#plus-bold" href="#plus-bold"></use></svg>
							<svg class="icon minus" focusable="false"><use xlink:href="#minus-bold" href="#minus-bold"></use></svg>
						</span>
					</a>
				</h3>
				<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents" id="anchor-id928">
					<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents-description">Bixby is Samsung’s intelligent voice assistant that can help you find answers, control your device and streamline your tasks. Bixby has received the following upgrades on Galaxy phones with Galaxy AI, enabling it to be a more helpful, context-aware assistant with greater natural language capability:
<br />⦁ General language understanding: Bixby can comprehend natural language, letting you ask freely and casually for what you want — almost like asking a person.
<br />⦁ Device Q&amp;A: Bixby can answer more questions about the actual device it’s built into, helping you figure out how certain settings or functions work or troubleshoot device issues like a device AI agent.
<br />⦁ Open Q&amp;A: Bixby can agentically search the web to find the right answers for you, meaning you can ask more questions on a wider variety of topics.<sup>15</sup></div>
					
					
						
					<!--
						<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents-disclaimer-wrap">
							<p class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents-disclaimer">...omitted...</p>
						</div>-->
						
					

					
				</div>
			</li>
		
			
			
			<li class="su12-accordion-faqs__item " an-tr="su12_accordion faqs-im marketing page-cta-content_click" an-ca="content click" an-ac="feature" an-la="faq:accordion:is galaxy ai secure in terms of privacy" role="listitem">
				<h3>
					<a href="javascript:void(0)" class="su12-accordion-faqs__title" aria-expanded="false" role="button">
						
						<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__title-text">Is Galaxy AI secure in terms of privacy?</div>
						<span class="icon-wrap">
							<svg class="icon plus" focusable="false"><use xlink:href="#plus-bold" href="#plus-bold"></use></svg>
							<svg class="icon minus" focusable="false"><use xlink:href="#minus-bold" href="#minus-bold"></use></svg>
						</span>
					</a>
				</h3>
				<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents" id="anchor-id1010">
					<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents-description">Yes, Galaxy AI is secure in terms of privacy. Samsung’s technology is built with security at its core, integrating both hardware and software protections to ensure that your personal data stays protected. As AI plays a bigger role in daily life, Samsung remains committed to protecting your personal information through strong, layered security. A few of the security measures related to Galaxy AI include:
<br />⦁ On Device Protection: For Galaxy AI data that gets processed on device, the Personal Data Engine ensures that your personal data is gathered and processed safely. It encrypts that data and saves it onto your device with KEEP and Knox Vault, making it harder for anyone else to gain access.
<br />⦁ Tailored Controls: Users can decide whether their Galaxy AI data gets processed locally on device or out in the cloud, letting them tailor their privacy settings to their preferences.
<br />⦁ Connected Security: Your connected Galaxy devices monitor each other for potential threats with Knox Matrix Trust Chain technology, adding another level of security for your data.<sup>16</sup></div>
					
					
						
					<!--
						<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents-disclaimer-wrap">
							<p class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents-disclaimer">...omitted...</p>
						</div>-->
						
					

					
				</div>
			</li>
		
	</ul>
</div>

  <script type="application/ld+json" data-type="seo" data-object-type="FAQPage" data-id="fc3baa7f-3499-43f8-a933-6d4423296a3a">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","@id":"https://www.samsung.com/pk/galaxy-ai/#FAQ","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"What devices have Galaxy AI?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Galaxy AI comes built into Samsung devices like smartphones, smartwatches, earbuds and tablets, although the available features vary by device.\r\n<br>\r\n<br>⦁ Galaxy AI is supported on smartphones starting from the S24 Series phones onward.\r\n<br>⦁ Galaxy AI is supported on tablets and wearable products (such as Galaxy Watch and Galaxy Buds), but the level of support depends on the model and OS version.\r\n<br>⦁ The availability of certain Galaxy AI features may vary by region as well as model. If you want to be sure of getting a certain Galaxy AI feature, check beforehand that it's provided on that particular model in your region.\r\n<br>⦁ Please note that the supported features and models may change with future product releases and updates."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How do I use Galaxy AI on my Samsung phone?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Galaxy AI comes built into various Samsung devices, though available features may vary by model. Some Galaxy AI features run automatically in the background, while others can be activated by tapping on the four-star Galaxy AI icon that appears in certain apps and screens.\r\n<br>⦁ Some Galaxy AI features run automatically by default, making them effortless to enjoy.\r\n<br>⦁ Some Galaxy AI features require user action. Tap the Galaxy AI icon that appears in certain apps and screens to bring up a list of relevant actions. Then tap the action you want, and it will be done for you instantly.\r\n<br>⦁ Certain Galaxy AI features can be customized to your preferences, so you can adjust to the experience you want. In addition to enabling and disabling features, you can choose how they function in certain situations and more."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What are the main features of Samsung’s Galaxy AI?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Galaxy AI provides a wide variety of features for personalization, productivity, creativity and communication, with some of the more prominent features being:\r\n<br>⦁ Photo Assist: Powerful editing tools in your Gallery that let you effortlessly get your photos looking the way you want.\r\n<br>⦁ Creative Studio: Creation tools that let you easily make custom content like personalized stickers.\r\n<br>⦁ Now Nudge: Recognizes what's happening on your screen to provide context-aware suggestions for your convenience, like shortcuts to your Calendar and Gallery apps.\r\n<br>⦁ Now Brief: Quick snapshots of useful info and insights delivered throughout the day to help keep you on track, including news, calendar events and personal recaps, along with personalized reminders and recommendations.\r\n<br>⦁ Interpreter: Real-time translations are delivered as audio to your Galaxy Buds and as text on your Galaxy phone.\r\n<br>⦁ Writing Assist: A writing and editing tool that lets you proofread, reformat, reword and summarize any text you’ve written or selected.\r\n<br>⦁ Bixby: A personal device assistant capable of natural, free-flowing conversation.<sup>1,2,5,6,10,12,15</sup>"}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What are the key Galaxy AI features of Samsung Galaxy S26 Ultra?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Samsung Galaxy S26 Ultra is powered by Galaxy AI to provide a smoother, more intelligent mobile experience and various tools for creation, communication, productivity and more, with some of the key features including:\r\n<br>\r\n<br>⦁ Photo Assist, which provides powerful image editing and creation tools for your photos.\r\n<br>⦁ Creative Studio, which lets you easily create custom content like personalized sticker sets.\r\n<br>⦁ Now Nudge, which recognizes what's happening on your screen to provide context-aware suggestions for your convenience, like shortcuts to your Calendar and Gallery apps.\r\n<br>⦁ Now Brief, which organizes insights and updates about your day in short, efficient briefs, allowing you to easily catch up on calendar events, news items, your daily activity and more, along with personalized reminders and recommendations.\r\n<br>⦁ Document Scan, which automatically detects and cleans up pictures of documents taken from your phone.\r\n<br>⦁ Bixby, Samsung’s personal device assistant that lets you give commands and ask for advice using natural language.<sup>1,2,5,6,11,15,18</sup>"}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What are the benefits of Samsung Galaxy AI for everyday users like me?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Galaxy AI makes your devices more intelligent, intuitive and context-aware, so they’re able to support you more naturally in everyday tasks and provide real actions for what you need. Not only that, Galaxy AI powers a wide range of useful tools and features that let you accomplish more tasks and work more efficiently on your device.\r\n<br>⦁ Context-aware assistance: Galaxy AI helps your device understand what’s going on, resulting in smarter assistance that helps streamline tasks and save time. For example, Now Nudge provides quick action prompts based on what it recognizes is happening on your screen.\r\n<br>⦁ Additional tools and features: Galaxy AI powers a whole host of additional features within your device, including creative tools like Photo Assist and Creative Studio, productivity tools like Transcript Assist and Writing Assist and communication tools like Interpreter.\r\n<br>⦁ More personalized insights: Galaxy AI also powers your device to provide more intelligent insights about yourself. You can get useful reminders and recaps about your day with Now Brief and deeper insights about your health in Energy Score.<sup>1,2,5,6,9,12,14</sup>"}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What languages does Galaxy AI support?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"As of March 2026, Galaxy AI's Photo Assist, Creative Studio and Writing Assist support 41 languages. Now Nudge and Recalled data for Now Brief support 13 languages. Call Assist (e.g. Live Translate), Note Assist, Interpreter, and Transcript Assist support 22 languages. Call Screening feature for Call Assist supports 13 languages.\r\n<br>\r\n<br>Full list of languages is below.\r\n<br>\r\n<br>⦁ Photo Assist supported languages: English, Spanish, Portuguese, German, French, Italian, Polish, Korean, Chinese (Simplified, Traditional), Japanese, Thai, Vietnamese, Arabic, Indonesian, Hindi, Russian, Turkish, Romanian, Swedish, Dutch, Czech, Danish, Finnish, Hungarian, Ukrainian, Hebrew, Greek, Serbian, Bulgarian, Croatian, Norwegian, Slovak, Lithuanian, Slovenian, Latvian, Estonian, Bengali, Swahili, Filipino and Gujarati.\r\n<br>⦁ Creative Studio supported languages: English, Spanish, Portuguese, German, French, Italian, Polish, Korean, Chinese (Simplified, Traditional), Japanese, Thai, Vietnamese, Arabic, Indonesian, Hindi, Russian, Turkish, Romanian, Swedish, Dutch, Czech, Danish, Finnish, Hungarian, Ukrainian, Hebrew, Greek, Serbian, Bulgarian, Croatian, Norwegian, Slovak, Lithuanian, Slovenian, Latvian, Estonian, Bengali, Swahili, Filipino and Gujarati.\r\n<br>⦁ Now Nudge supported languages: Korean, English, Spanish, Italian, German, French, Portuguese, Polish, Chinese (Simplified), Japanese, Thai, Hindi and Vietnamese.\r\n<br>⦁ Recalled data for Now Brief supported languages: Korean, English, Spanish, Italian, German, French, Portuguese, Polish, Chinese (Simplified), Japanese, Thai, Hindi and Vietnamese.\r\n<br>⦁ Call Assist (e.g. Live Translate), Note Assist, Interpreter, and Transcript Assist supported languages: Korean, English, Spanish, French, German, Italian, Portuguese, Chinese, Japanese, Polish, Hindi, Thai, Vietnamese, Arabic, Indonesian, Russian, Turkish, Dutch, Swedish, Romanian, Filipino and Gujarati.\r\n<br>⦁ Call Screening feature for Call Assist supported languages: English, Portuguese, Spanish, French, German, Italian, Chinese (Simplified), Japanese, Korean, Thai, Polish, Vietnamese and Hindi.\r\n<br>⦁ Writing Assist supported languages: English, Portuguese, Spanish, French, Korean, German, Italian, Chinese (Simplified, Traditional), Japanese, Hindi, Polish, Thai, Vietnamese, Arabic, Russian, Indonesian, Turkish, Dutch, Swedish, Romanian, Czech, Danish, Finnish, Hungarian, Ukrainian, Hebrew, Greek, Serbian, Bulgarian, Croatian, Norwegian, Slovak, Lithuanian, Slovenian, Latvian, Estonian, Bengali, Swahili, Filipino and Gujarati."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How does having a good AI phone improve my everyday mobile experiences?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"A good AI phone helps everyday mobile experiences flow more smoothly by understanding your personal context to provide more intuitive interactions and personalized assistance. In addition, AI can unlock various features that let you do more on your phone, whether it’s for work tasks or personal creative pursuits. Here are a few ways Galaxy AI enhances the mobile experience on Samsung smartphones:\r\n<br>⦁ Intuitive interactions: Galaxy AI helps your phone better understand what’s happening, so you can find or achieve what you need faster with features like Now Nudge. \r\n<br>⦁ Personalized assistance: Galaxy AI grasps your patterns and preferences to deliver information that’s more useful and relevant to you, like tailored insights with Now Brief and a more detailed Energy Score.\r\n<br>⦁ Creative tools: Galaxy AI powers various creative tools like Photo Assist and Creative Studio, allowing you to edit, design and create like a professional on your phone.\r\n<br>⦁ Productivity tools: Galaxy AI also powers various useful tools for work and study, like Transcript Assist and Writing Assist, which can help summarize and organize large amounts of information in no time.<sup>1,2,5,6,7,9,12,14</sup>"}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How do Samsung Galaxy phones improve photo quality with AI?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Samsung Galaxy phones improve photo quality with AI through the following methods:\r\n<br>⦁ AI ProVisual Engine: Samsung’s advanced image processor is powered by AI to enhance photo quality. AI ProVisual Engine intelligently analyzes and refines every frame for clarity, color and detail. The result is stunningly accurate, true-to-life photos and videos, even when taken at night or from a distance.\r\n<br>⦁ AI ISP: Samsung combines its Image Signal Processor (ISP) with AI to automatically optimize each shot in real time for clearer, more detailed images. AI ISP has now been applied to the front camera as well in Samsung Galaxy S26 Ultra to produce more natural, realistic selfies when pictures are snapped from the front.<sup>19</sup>"}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How do I use the translation feature on Samsung Galaxy Buds?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"To hear translations spoken directly into your Samsung Galaxy Buds, you can use the Interpreter feature through the following steps:\r\n<br>⦁ Open the Interpreter app on your phone. You may have to download the appropriate language pack for the language of the person you’re speaking with.\r\n<br>⦁ Place your Galaxy Buds in your ears.\r\n<br>⦁ Tap the microphone icon that appears on your phone’s screen. In Listening Mode, the microphone icon appears at the bottom of the screen. In Conversation Mode, there are two microphone icons that appear on screen, one for each of the languages being translated.\r\n<br>⦁ Allow the Interpreter app to listen to your conversation partner as they speak in a different language. You may have to select for your desired languages.\r\n<br>⦁ The spoken translation will be delivered to your Galaxy Buds. In addition, the transcribed text will also be displayed on the screen of your phone, so you can read along as you listen.\r\n<br>⦁ You can also pause, resume and play back the recording using the touch controls of your Galaxy Buds.<sup>10</sup>"}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What are the latest AI upgrades for Bixby on Samsung Galaxy phones?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Bixby is Samsung’s intelligent voice assistant that can help you find answers, control your device and streamline your tasks. Bixby has received the following upgrades on Galaxy phones with Galaxy AI, enabling it to be a more helpful, context-aware assistant with greater natural language capability:\r\n<br>⦁ General language understanding: Bixby can comprehend natural language, letting you ask freely and casually for what you want — almost like asking a person.\r\n<br>⦁ Device Q&A: Bixby can answer more questions about the actual device it’s built into, helping you figure out how certain settings or functions work or troubleshoot device issues like a device AI agent.\r\n<br>⦁ Open Q&A: Bixby can agentically search the web to find the right answers for you, meaning you can ask more questions on a wider variety of topics.<sup>15</sup>"}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is Galaxy AI secure in terms of privacy?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes, Galaxy AI is secure in terms of privacy. Samsung’s technology is built with security at its core, integrating both hardware and software protections to ensure that your personal data stays protected. As AI plays a bigger role in daily life, Samsung remains committed to protecting your personal information through strong, layered security. A few of the security measures related to Galaxy AI include:\r\n<br>⦁ On Device Protection: For Galaxy AI data that gets processed on device, the Personal Data Engine ensures that your personal data is gathered and processed safely. It encrypts that data and saves it onto your device with KEEP and Knox Vault, making it harder for anyone else to gain access.\r\n<br>⦁ Tailored Controls: Users can decide whether their Galaxy AI data gets processed locally on device or out in the cloud, letting them tailor their privacy settings to their preferences.\r\n<br>⦁ Connected Security: Your connected Galaxy devices monitor each other for potential threats with Knox Matrix Trust Chain technology, adding another level of security for your data.<sup>16</sup>"}}]}</script>


</div>
<div class="cm-g-text-block aem-GridColumn aem-GridColumn--default--12">





  
	<div class="textblock    bg-white  text-left  text-mo-left container-width-medium">
		
		
    	
    	
    	
    	<div class="textblock__body padding-top--48 padding-bottom--48">
				
				
			
			
			
			
			
			
			
			<div class="textblock__disclaimer">
				
				<ul class="textblock__disclaimer-list" role="list">
            		<li class="textblock__disclaimer-text" role="listitem">* Samsung Account login may be required to use certain AI features.</li>
            	
            		<li class="textblock__disclaimer-text" role="listitem"><br />* Samsung does not make any promises, assurances or guarantees as to the accuracy, completeness or reliability of the output provided by AI features. </li>
            	
            		<li class="textblock__disclaimer-text" role="listitem"><br />* Availability of Galaxy AI features may vary depending on the region/country, OS/One UI version, device model and phone carrier.</li>
            	
            		<li class="textblock__disclaimer-text" role="listitem"><br />* Galaxy AI basic features provided by Samsung are free. Future releases may include enhanced features or new services that are offered on a paid basis. Different terms may apply for AI features provided by third parties. Galaxy AI basic features are those services listed under &quot;Advanced intelligence&quot; in the current Samsung Services Terms and Conditions.</li>
            	
            		<li class="textblock__disclaimer-text" role="listitem"><br />* Galaxy AI service may be limited for minors in certain regions with age restrictions over AI usage.</li>
            	
            		<li class="textblock__disclaimer-text" role="listitem"><br />* Full list of supported languages for Galaxy AI features can be found in the FAQ section.</li>
            	
            		<li class="textblock__disclaimer-text" role="listitem"><br />* Photo Assist may require a network connection and Samsung Account login. Service availability may vary by country, language or device model. Photo Assist may result in a resized photo. A visible watermark is overlaid on the image output upon saving in order to indicate that the image is generated by AI. The accuracy and reliability of the generated output is not guaranteed.</li>
            	
            		<li class="textblock__disclaimer-text" role="listitem"><br />* Image simulated. Actual UX/UI may differ. Availability of colors, sizes, models, and watch bands may vary by country or carrier. Products sold separately.</li>
            	
            		<li class="textblock__disclaimer-text" role="listitem"><br />1. Photo Assist may require a network connection and Samsung Account login. Service availability may vary by country, language or device model. Photo Assist may result in a resized photo. A visible watermark is overlaid on the image output upon saving in order to indicate that the image is generated by AI. The accuracy and reliability of the generated output is not guaranteed.</li>
            	
            		<li class="textblock__disclaimer-text" role="listitem"><br />2. Creative Studio feature requires a network connection and Samsung Account login. Service availability may vary by country, language or device model. The accuracy and reliability of the generated output is not guaranteed. Sticker sets only compatible with Samsung keyboard and can only be shared via Quick Share feature with other Galaxy devices that have One UI 5.0 or later installed and Quick Share app version 13.8.50.x or later.</li>
            	
            		<li class="textblock__disclaimer-text" role="listitem"><br />3. Results may vary per video depending on how sounds present in the video. Samsung Account login required. Six types of sound can be detected; voices, music, wind, nature, crowd and noise. The actual sound detection may vary depending on audio source, and the condition of the video. Accuracy of results is not guaranteed. Certain types of sound can be detected, such as voices, music, wind, nature, crowd and noise. On certain apps, Audio Eraser in the Quick Panel adjusts separated audio source volumes in real time without copying, modifying or storing the original content.</li>
            	
            		<li class="textblock__disclaimer-text" role="listitem"><br />4. Maximum length per clip to be edited using Auto Trim for Photo Assist is 90 minutes. Maximum length of combined clips to be edited using Auto Trim for Photo Assist is 180 minutes. Maximum number of clips to be edited per video project is 60 clips. Accuracy of results is not guaranteed.</li>
            	
            		<li class="textblock__disclaimer-text" role="listitem"><br />5.  Now Nudge feature requires a Samsung Account login. Available functions and features may vary by country, region and language. Text message prompts available with certain third party messaging apps including Samsung Messages, Google Messages, Google Chat. Based on availability at the time of product launch. May change without notice. Share photos in Now Nudge works by analyzing available image content. Accuracy of results is not guaranteed.</li>
            	
            		<li class="textblock__disclaimer-text" role="listitem"><br />6. Now Brief feature requires Samsung Account login. Service availability may vary by country, language, device model, apps. Some features may require a network connection. The description of photos provided by moments may not align with the user's intent. Events schedule notification is supported with calendar apps that utilize Android calendar database and available if Samsung Calendar is installed. Notifications for dog walking require SmartTag2 and Pet Care in SmartThings to be activated. SmartTag2 sold separately. Notifications must be switched on to be used as the recalled data. Recalled data available from supported app notifications, Messages, Gmail and Samsung Wallet and data collected from Gmail is only applicable if the user consents to Personal Data Intelligent's Gmail read permission. Recalled data for reservation details only available from reservation confirmation messages.</li>
            	
            		<li class="textblock__disclaimer-text" role="listitem"><br />8. Call Screening feature for Call Assist may vary by country, region and language. Feature needs to be manually activated.</li>
            	
            		<li class="textblock__disclaimer-text" role="listitem"><br />9. Transcription and Summary features for Transcript Assist require a network connection and Samsung Account login. Features for Transcript Assist only available on the pre-installed Samsung Voice Recorder app or files recorded using the pre-installed Samsung Phone app, Samsung Notes app or Samsung Interpreter app. Voice recording feature in the pre-installed Samsung Phone app may not be supported in some countries. Audio files must be under 3 hours in duration to be processed. Summarizing feature for Transcript Assist can be activated when a certain number of characters is met. Service availability may vary by language. Accuracy of results is not guaranteed.</li>
            	
            		<li class="textblock__disclaimer-text" role="listitem"><br />10. Interpreter feature requires Samsung Account login. Certain languages may require language pack download. Service availability may vary by language. Accuracy of results is not guaranteed. Availability and supported features may vary by country, region or carrier. Availability of supported languages may vary.</li>
            	
            		<li class="textblock__disclaimer-text" role="listitem"><br />11. Document area within the camera screen must be greater than 20%. If the document contains only images without text, it may not be recognized as a document in Photo Mode. Original document must be rectangular. All four corners of the document must be visible within the camera screen without any obstructions. Capture angle must be within 20 degrees after setting to 0 degrees when the document surface and the camera are level. Correction for folding is possible within two turns and between 130 and 180 degrees. For warped documents, the document must be placed on the floor with a uniformly short-axis angle of A4 size, with a distance of less than 4 cm between the floor and the document. Traces may remain after shadow removal for documents with strong shadows or colors. A gap greater than 0.8 cm between objects (text, tables, images, etc.) and obstructions (fingers, folded edges) must be present. Not supported if the object and obstacle are not separated or overlap. Moiré removal restrictions may result in residual moiré in cases of very strong moiré. Document-specific filters may produce unintended results when applied to scenes where the document is not visible. Available Saved File format is JPEG or PDF. Available Multi-Scan Image Import Input File Format is JPEG, HEIC, PNG, BMP, WebP or GIF. Available Gallery Scan Input File Format is JPEG or HEIF (JPG, HEIC). Usage may be limited in certain temperatures.</li>
            	
            		<li class="textblock__disclaimer-text" role="listitem"><br />12. Writing Assist requires a network connection and Samsung Account login. Must meet length requirements to activate feature. Service availability may vary by language. Accuracy of results is not guaranteed.</li>
            	
            		<li class="textblock__disclaimer-text" role="listitem"><br />13. Bedtime guidance is available on Android phone (Android 11 and above) requires Samsung Health app (v6.30.2 or later). Samsung account login required. Bedtime guidance is based on 3 days of sleep analysis of user's circadian rhythm and sleep pressure. Sleep features are intended for general wellness and fitness purposes only. Not intended for use in detection, diagnosis, treatment of any medical condition or sleep disorder. The measurements are for your personal reference only. Please consult a medical professional for advice.</li>
            	
            		<li class="textblock__disclaimer-text" role="listitem"><br />14. Energy Score is available on Android phones (Android 11 or above) and requires Samsung Health app (v6.27 or above). Samsung Account login required. Service availability may vary by country, region, language. To check the Energy Score, the health data tracked from Samsung Galaxy Watch (Galaxy Watch4 Series and later models using OS 5.0 or above) or Samsung Galaxy Ring must be synchronized with the Samsung Health App. Needs at least the previous day’s activity data and sleep, and heart rate data during sleep. Not intended for use in detection, diagnosis, treatment of any medical condition. The result is for your personal reference only. Please consult a medical professional for advice.</li>
            	
            		<li class="textblock__disclaimer-text" role="listitem"><br />15. Bixby service availability requires Samsung Account login and data connection. Available functions and features may vary by country, region, and language. Bixby only recognizes certain accents and dialects of English (UK), English (US), English (India), French (France), German (Germany), Italian (Italy), Japanese (Japan), Korean (South Korea), Mandarin Chinese (China), Spanish (Spain), Portuguese (Brazil) and Spanish (Latin America). Other supported languages may be added in the future. Not all accents, dialects, and expressions may be recognized, and actual performance may vary depending on pronunciation, voice level, and the surrounding environment. Use of Bixby may be limited in certain situations such as when recording media (Video/Game/Voice), during calls, Maximum Power Saving mode, Emergency mode and Samsung Kids. Service availability may vary by country/service provider/language/device model/OS version. Bixby controls selected apps, other apps to be supported. To control SmartThings enabled devices with Bixby, first connect the devices to the SmartThings app. For more information, visit the SmartThings website (www.samsung.com/smartthings).</li>
            	
            		<li class="textblock__disclaimer-text" role="listitem"><br />16. The Personal Data Engine functions under the condition that the Personal Data Intelligence menu is on. Analyzed data will be deleted once the Personal Data Intelligence menu is turned off. Personal Data Engine recognizes select languages and certain accents/dialects, including but not limited to Arabic, (Simplified) Chinese, Dutch, English, French, German, Hindi, Indonesian, Italian, Japanese, Korean, Polish, Portuguese, Romanian, Russian, Spanish, Swedish, Thai, Turkish, and Vietnamese. Personal Data Engine currently analyzes Samsung native applications and supported app notifications. KEEP is available on Galaxy smartphones and tablets with One UI 8 or later.</li>
            	
            		<li class="textblock__disclaimer-text" role="listitem"><br />17. Knox Matrix is supported on Galaxy smartphones and tablets One UI 7.0 or above. Availability may vary by country or region.</li>
            	
            		<li class="textblock__disclaimer-text" role="listitem"><br />18. Service availability may vary by language. Accuracy of results is not guaranteed.</li>
            	
            		<li class="textblock__disclaimer-text" role="listitem"><br />19. Results may vary depending on light condition and/or shooting conditions including multiple subjects, being out of focus or moving subjects.</li>
            	</ul>
			</div>
		</div>
	</div>
	

</div>













